==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|phthisis}}, from {{der|en|grc|φθίσις||consumption, decline, wasting away}}, from {{m|grc|φθίω||I waste away}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈ(f)θaɪsɪs/|/ˈtaɪsɪs/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-phthisis.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-phthisis2.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|phthi|sis}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|phthises}}

# {{lb|en|archaic}} An [[atrophy]] of the [[body]] or part of the body, especially pulmonary [[tuberculosis]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c.1830-40's|passage=For some months to my becoming acquainted with him, his physicians had declared him in a confirmed '''phthisis'''. It was his custom, indeed, to speak calmly of his approaching dissolution, as a matter neither to be avoided nor regretted.|author=
Edgar Allan Poe|title=The Facts in the Case of M. Valdemar:Complete Stories and Poems of Edgar Allan Poe}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1985|passage=Tired from his journey and his chronic lung weakness, which he had saved from turning to '''phthisis''' by winter sojourns in Egypt, he was yet goodhumoured enough when his deputy reported the arrival of a gang of Jews who wanted judgment on something or someone.|author=Anthony Burgess|title=Kingdom of the Wicked}}

